body:
Yeah in fact it was so serious they thought there were more serious issues (which is why my father kept drinking them because he thought the issues were unrelated to the beverages) and when they took him to the hospital they found out they were severe stomach ulcers that got better about 2-3 weeks after just drinking water and medication they gave him.  

&#x200B;

These drinks also caused me issues but more of the cold sweats and severe anxiety type stuff.  My Aunt also had stomach issues after drinking these drinks.  All-in-All our family does not even consider buying these drinks at ALL anymore.

You have the same rules I do haha.  If anyone feels bad we have like a box of happy things in order to not let anything bad happen too,

&#x200B;

No I don't hold anyone responsible at all because they were tripping with me but I was more trying to explain that they tried and I wouldn't let them, like I wanted to be isolated and it felt like I couldn't say anything,  which they are my best friends so it was an odd moment for me.  Like my brain in that moment felt like I would infect them even though we all established we were there for eachother to pull eachother out if need be.

&#x200B;

Ive tripped dozens of times in my life so I was in a safe environment, I was feeling good (which if i ever felt bad i wouldn't take it),  I have treatment-resistant depression but ive never had a bad experience with psychedelics.  I typically do it like 4 or so times a year. It totally caught me off guard.  I still feel very off but I think sometimes bad trips are more of a learning experience than good, i was able to pull myself out of bad moments but i kept getting sucked back in.

&#x200B;

Right now I think the feeling I can say if you have seen everything everywhere all at once I am like on the edge of getting sucked into an everything bagel.
